{"title":"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many of the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/d/72d85c6959aaabfff6e0104544ff25c1445f3f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"23\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/a/62a76677add1d246708c86edfc7c4b8a40184914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/2/8b239c9d19fc9eacc595d2d8f307b6ee83d124a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"39\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/0/360df382578e9befa948ec29a4f999c84ec20aca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"39\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are to the left of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b31b51deaa1a9e903d120a02141556c3e70e348.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" /> when placed on the number line?\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/4/c747e5f60aa900b2aac94a987e0d9391937107f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 3 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 2 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 1 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 5 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"388\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can simply see which numbers are less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b31b51deaa1a9e903d120a02141556c3e70e348.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" /> (since the numbers that are less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b31b51deaa1a9e903d120a02141556c3e70e348.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" /> will be to the left of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b31b51deaa1a9e903d120a02141556c3e70e348.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />), and then count to see how many numbers satisfy the condition.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/9/09952e81bf7ff15cd0939cfba24ae6cbb2a23258.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-4 &lt; -3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/9/699fff7d19e56dfb6d0ddbaa8cc7dac36a460535.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2 &gt; -3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/a/92a6acbaf6bcf5873568a1d1399358ba6c31b587.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3.5 &lt; -3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"87\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/296f73bf7866cbe21ce349ec9f5630c834f39160.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2.5 &gt; -3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"87\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/0/be0a7cddfb06c234f125b2f7c0e5adfb594f46c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 &gt; 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Of these numbers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/d/ded7ca920878d2329d5cf87266010c2418d9707d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"57\" height=\"30\" /> of them would be to the left of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b31b51deaa1a9e903d120a02141556c3e70e348.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal (page does not exist)\">2025 CEMC Pascal</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Pro